  "preamble": "In Southern Min (Hokkien, Teochew), Pu-Xian and Hainan Min, nasal codas after open vowels disappeared in the vernacular layer, leaving the preceding vowel nasalized, so Proto-Min *-ɑm surfaces as [ã]: 三 'three', Proto-Min *sɑmA, is sã¹ in Jieyang and Xiamen. The literary (reading) layer keeps the coda [-m], which gives doublets such as Hokkien saⁿ / sam for 三. After close vowels the coda is kept, as in 南 Jieyang nam.",
